c9c|n|Light, familiar talk; conversation; gossip. ; A bird of the genus Icteria, allied to the warblers, in America. The best known species are the yellow-breasted chat (I. viridis), and the long-tailed chat (I. longicauda). In Europe the name is given to several birds of the family Saxicolidae, as the stonechat, and whinchat. ; A twig, cone, or little branch. See Chit. ; Small stones with ore.	a:1n2x,53,9;17jn,50,8;iqv,45,3;12f3,44,2;1o4m,35,6;1p1g,26,2;18l6,20,4~1n2x,53,9;17jn,50,8;1o4m,35,6;18l6,20,4;iqv,45,3;1p1g,26,2;12f3,44,2	v:iqv,49,4~iqv,49,4	V:2b5,12,1~2b5,12,1	n:1uno,9,4;29d5,6,1;1n1q,2,6~1n1q,2,6;1uno,9,4;29d5,6,1	N:1slg,81,6;1sl5,68,52;1vj7,66,8;l8b,1,1~1sl5,68,52;1vj7,66,8;1slg,81,6;l8b,1,1
